NOTE ON RUNNER LIMITATION (root cause of the two test-execution reds below):
  The active global developer dir is CommandLineTools:
    `xcode-select -p` => /Library/Developer/CommandLineTools
  Switching it (`sudo xcode-select -s`) requires root; `sudo` is password-gated and
  unavailable in this sandbox ("sudo: a password is required"). The CoreSimulator /
  testmanagerd diagnostics subprocess therefore cannot resolve `xcrun simctl`
  ("unable to find utility simctl"), which destabilizes the iOS-Simulator UI-test
  harness. There is also no code-signing identity in this sandbox
  (CODE_SIGNING_ALLOWED=NO), so host app-install for `platform=macOS` test launch fails.
  These are runner limitations, not surface defects.

